# HatchAI checks

These are local software checks. They do not upload images, contact an ESP32,
operate relays, test physical movement or certify electrical/thermal safety.

## Firmware and SPIFFS

    platformio run -e esp32dev
    platformio run -e esp32dev --target buildfs

The main project uses RelayThermostat. Obsolete PID examples and their tests
were archived during deployment cleanup; current regression tests remain here.

## Compiler-evaluated control checks

    xtensa-esp32-elf-g++ -std=c++14 -Iinclude -fsyntax-only test/automatic_control_compile_test.cpp test/thermostat_compile_test.cpp test/turn_cycle_compile_test.cpp

These compile the actual production control functions, adding constexpr annotations
under C++14; normal firmware still builds with C++11. They evaluate sensor recovery
and staleness, unfiltered alarm thresholds/hysteresis/ACK, low-warning timing,
calendar validation, RTC reservations/lockdown, motor exclusion/gap/deadlines,
thermostat threshold equality/hold behavior, minimum OFF time, sensor recovery,
manual mode, absence of periodic pulses and millis rollover. The tests use the same thermostat implementation as the main firmware. These do not emulate
GPIO, NVS, SHT40 I2C waveforms, RTC hardware or blocking peripheral timing.

## Node and isolated browser checks

    node test/control_dual_motor_test.cjs
    node test/ui-regression.cjs

The Node fixture checks calibrated durations, payload validation, independent
intervals, forced fan/false continuous-motor requests, URL encoding, session-token
actions, shared API serialization and server-error messages.

The browser script serves assets on an ephemeral loopback port, uses isolated
storage/fake time and mocks every ESP32 API. It checks existing Wi-Fi scan/join/
forget behavior, duplicate/unsafe SSIDs, two batch slots and legacy record
preservation, dashboard updates without blinking, independent motor timing,
queued runs/Stop, calibrated saved intervals/durations, direct sliders in both modes,
Both-roller conflicts, editable day-18 turning end, rejected actions, firmware compatibility and responsive layouts.
It also checks applying/resetting temperature calibration and failure feedback.

Chrome and Playwright are required. On this workstation:

    $env:HATCH_PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE='C:/Users/LENOVO/AppData/Roaming/npm/node_modules/@playwright/cli/node_modules/playwright-core'

Optionally set `HATCH_UI_SCREENSHOT_DIR` for screenshots. The script reports the
actual check count on completion. JavaScript syntax and asset-size checks must
also be run when web files change. Physical testing and uploads require separate
authorization. Follow docs/SD_RECOVERY.md for the current power-loss policy and
14-case physical test procedure, and docs/INTEGRATED_CONTROL.md for thermostat details.

## SD recovery additions

    python test/recovery_fault_simulation.py
    node test/recovery-ui.cjs

Include test/recovery_compile_test.cpp and test/session_policy_compile_test.cpp
in the C++14 compiler-evaluated command.
It checks the actual CRC vector, RTC day/lockdown boundaries, snapshot candidate
selection, motor journal/position guards and reconciliation predicates.
The Python test uses temporary host files and a documented fault model; it does
not execute the full ESP32 JSON/SD driver. The recovery browser test covers the component modal, automatic clock sync/throttling, SD fault/pending/verified distinctions, Both-batch import and exceptional position confirmation using mocked APIs.
No physical brownout, card removal, RTC battery or mains-load test is implied.

## Manual roller update

See docs/MANUAL_ROLLER_CONTROL.md. Browser regressions include active-batch
roller selection, duplicate-roller rejection, actual batch labels, settings
review and manual controls during mocked SD recovery faults. Thermostat compiler
checks cover manual ON after the five-second OFF guard and immediate OFF.
Recovery compiler checks cover legacy/current sensor timing compatibility.
These do not validate physical relay/SD/LCD behavior or run controller NVS
transactions on hardware.

## Roller requests, cards and LCD update

Include test/batch_display_compile_test.cpp in the compiler-evaluated command.
It checks no/single/two/shared batch selection for the physical estimate row.
Browser tests cover card-click details, in-modal Edit/Delete, Done confirmation,
cancel/rejection/history retention and direct timed runs with automatic climate
ON during a mocked SD fault. No physical outputs are exercised.

## Heating and sensor/SD recovery

Include sensor_sampling_compile_test.cpp with thermostat_compile_test.cpp and automatic_control_compile_test.cpp for failed-read cadence, rollover, cold-dip filtering, startup qualification versus normal valid temperature changes, stale shutdown and raw hot/critical shutdown. Browser checks cover the heater OFF reason and transient read diagnostics with mocked payloads; they do not execute controller SD/NVS recovery transactions. See docs/HEATING_SENSOR_SD_FIX.md.

Concurrent slider update: the production restart-dwell predicate is per motor (canStart), journals allow two live intents with independent ownership, and overlapping timer tests verify that a lower deadline leaves upper remaining time unchanged. Browser checks retain the existing sliders without combined buttons and verify each Stop leaves the peer ON. Earlier one-motor-at-a-time assumptions are superseded. Physical simultaneous motor load and SD/NVS power-cut tests remain unperformed.

SHT40 version: include sht40_protocol_compile_test.cpp in the C++14 compiler checks. This checks the published CRC vector, independent temperature/RH corruption, frame length, conversion endpoints and RH clamping. Driver I2C presence/read-timeout paths require mocked transport or physical testing; compilation alone is not sensor validation.
